scope: Network+ final boot fix. Chris PASS at 82cf3d623, RETROACTIVE: I shipped 9ae8cc25f with --skip-chris because production was 100 percent broken (the exam could not start), then requested the gate. He ruled the skip defensible (pre-existing audited mechanism, used twice before; my audit entries matched what he verified) and confirmed FirebaseAuth.waitForAuth() is the platform-standard primitive AccessGuard already uses three times. He mutation-tested my new assertions against the pre-fix page and re-curled production: SHA byte-identical to the repo.

CORRECTED MECHANISM, because my first two commit messages got it wrong: callFunction is exported at FirebaseAuth.js:737 and is ALWAYS defined, so the page guard passed. init() is deferred to DOMContentLoaded at :744 while the exam inline script runs synchronously, so the module-level functions handle was still null and callFunction itself threw 'Firebase Functions not initialized'. NOT 'callFunction undefined', and NOT the 'Cloud Functions unavailable' string I twice reported the student saw.

RESIDUAL, OPEN as taskboard 439, not fixed here: if the Firebase SDK fails to load, loadFirebaseSDK() returns false, init() returns without registering onAuthStateChanged, _authReadyResolve() is never called, and waitForAuth() never settles, so the page hangs forever with no error. The OLD code failed FAST on that input. The boot fix traded a guaranteed visible failure for a silent hang there. Both states are broken; one tells the student. It is in the SHARED component, so the fix belongs there.

ALSO OPEN: taskboard 440 (lint rule: a callable invoked on page load must be downstream of waitForAuth) and 438 (netfinal suites wired into no deploy gate). And the one neither gate can close: NO REAL STUDENT SITTING HAS BEEN VERIFIED. Chris verified serving; I verified the request now leaves the browser at the right moment. Neither is a student starting an exam.

